Upstream: https://github.com/official-stockfish/Stockfish
Pinned commit: edb0d9db6731067ec50ce619ff372b463bc4dd5d (sf_19).

Chromatique modifications, made in October and November 2026, replace static evaluation with
the project's own trained network, add learned move-ordering policy, preserve
the raw en-passant/repetition feature contract, and prohibit Stockfish NNUE
evaluation. v4.1.0 uses independently learned value and policy first-layer encoders,
while retaining the project's fully neural evaluation and policy contract.
Standalone release packaging adds version identification and executable-relative model discovery.
Search and evaluation mathematics are unchanged by that packaging.
Modified files are listed in release.json and the complete diff against the pinned upstream is in docs/stockfish-changes.patch.

The complete corresponding engine source, build system, model in editable JSON
and native format, and original copyright/license notices are distributed here.
The stock Stockfish NNUE network and any external game/puzzle datasets are not
included. The bundled model is Chromatique's own network.

The src/incbin helper retains its upstream UNLICENCE.
